    "https://wd105.myworkdaysite.com/recruiting/federation/Federation_Careers/job/Ballarat-Victoria/Casual---TAFE-Teacher--Corrections_JR100766-1": {
      "title": "Casual",
      "description": "Casual - TAFE Teacher, Corrections Skip to main content Federation Careers Sign In Working at Federation Search for Jobs Introduce Yourself Casual - TAFE Teacher, Corrections page is loaded Casual - TAFE Teacher, Corrections Apply locations Ballarat, Victoria time type Part time posted on Posted 30+ Days Ago time left to apply End Date: January 31, 2027 (30+ days left to apply) job requisition id JR100766 TAFE Teacher at Cert IV TAE with 2 or more years Vocational Experience and 1 to 2 years Education experience Position closing date: 30/01/2027 Ranked number one university in Australia for First Generation Student Enrolments (Good Universities Guide 2022) and with top rankings in Victoria around student support, social equity, skills and employment, we are driven to make difference to every student and the community providing lifelong learning, skills, and research locally, regionally, and globally. With University and TAFE campuses in Ballarat, Berwick, Gippsland, and the Wimmera we are positioned to provide pathways from vocational education and skills training through to higher education. Federation TAFE – Barwon Southwest or Grampians Region Prisons Casual appointment Rates of pay will vary according to the qualifications held and nature of the work undertaken About the role Responsible for the development, teaching and assessment of TAFE programs at Corrections facilities in the Barwon Southwest or Grampians region. You will: conduct assessments within Corrections related programs; develop innovative learning activities and assessment strategies; use a wide range of teaching and assessment strategies; and prepare, deliver and administer vocational training and education programs. About you To be considered for this position, you will have demonstrated: a Certificate IV in Training and Assessment or a diploma or higher-level qualification in adult education; possession of a vocational qualification relevant to the trade; vocational experience with the ability to plan, prepare, deliver and assess training programs; exemplary communication and interpersonal skills; and ability to effectively utilise online learning platforms and technologies. Please note you may apply for casual work at any time. You may also change your details or withdraw from the casual register through the \"Candidate profile\". How to apply Applicants are required to submit a copy of your resume and relevant teaching qualification. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are encouraged to apply Federation University is committed to The Circle Back Initiative program, whereby we will respond to every applicant. If you are experiencing technical difficulties with your application, please email the Recruitment team or phone 03 5327 9756. Our position descriptions also list a contact person for job specific inquiries. Let our staff tell you more. 0:00 / 4:17 About us Established in 1870 Federation University has been reaching communities and building generations of independent thinkers united in the knowledge that they are greater together. Federation University is committed to attracting, developing and retaining the best talent ranging from our academic and research staff to those working in student experience and professional roles. We are all part of a collaborative culture inspiring the highest levels of excellence, innovation, integrity and respect. Read More Follow Us Federation University Information Privacy Procedure © 2026 Workday, Inc. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://wd105.myworkdaysite.com/recruiting/federation/Federation_Careers/job/Casual-Opportunities_JR100001": {
