    "https://wd105.myworkdaysite.com/recruiting/federation/Federation_Careers/job/Mt-Helen-Campus/Business-Manager--Co-op-Community-Clinics_JR101506": {
      "title": "Business Manager, Co-op Community Clinics",
      "description": "Business Manager, Co-op Community Clinics Skip to main content Federation Careers Sign In Working at Federation Search for Jobs Introduce Yourself Business Manager, Co-op Community Clinics page is loaded Business Manager, Co-op Community Clinics Apply locations Mt Helen Campus time type Full time posted on Posted 6 Days Ago time left to apply End Date: September 28, 2026 (12 days left to apply) job requisition id JR101506 Drive the growth, sustainability and impact of Federation University’s Co-op Community Clinics. •\tInstitute of Health and Wellbeing – Mt Helen or Churchill Campus •\tFull-time, continuing appointment •\tHEW 8 - $117,650 p.a. plus up to 17% superannuation Position closing date: 27/09/2026 Ranked number one university in Australia for First Generation Student Enrolments (Good Universities Guide 2022) and with top rankings in Victoria around student support, social equity, skills and employment, we are driven to make difference to every student and the community providing lifelong learning, skills, and research locally, regionally, and globally. With University and TAFE campuses in Ballarat, Berwick, Gippsland, and the Wimmera we are positioned to provide pathways from vocational education and skills training through to higher education. About the role As Business Manager, Co-op Community Clinics, you will drive the operational success, sustainability and growth of Federation University’s multidisciplinary teaching clinics. You will oversee business performance, governance, quality and service improvement, while strengthening partnerships that expand community impact and enhance student learning. Working with academic and clinical leaders, you will identify business opportunities, develop partnerships, business cases and funding proposals, and implement systems that strengthen efficiency, consistency and long-term sustainability. You will also help grow community engagement, improve client experience and supporting innovative models of service delivery. You will: support the planning, growth and ongoing success of all co-op clinics; contribute to the development and management of budgets; ensure all clinics operate in accordance with university policy, legislative requirements and relevant regulatory frameworks; and develop, implement and continuously improve clinic policies, procedures and governance frameworks across all clinic disciplines. About you Reporting to the Deputy Dean you will have demonstrated experience in operational and business management within a complex service environment, including planning, service development and improving performance. You will draw on your knowledge and experience in health services operations to identifying and develop opportunities that support service and business growth. You will possess: experience in financial management, including budgeting, forecasting, reporting and resource allocation to support sustainable operations; ability to develop, implement and review policies, procedures, governance frameworks and systems; experience leading, managing and developing staff, fostering a collaborative, customer-focused and high-performing team culture; ability to establish and maintain productive relationships with stakeholders, and to develop partnerships that support organisational objectives; and highly developed analytical, problem-solving and decision-making skills, with the capacity to manage competing priorities and complex operational issues. All University positions must hold a valid Employer Working With Children Check (WWCC). Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are encouraged to apply How to apply Please apply by Sunday, 27 September 2026. Applicants are required to submit a resume and a response to the key selection criteria. View position description Federation University is committed to The Circle Back Initiative program, whereby we will respond to every applicant. If you are experiencing technical difficulties with your application, please email the Recruitment team or phone 03 5327 9756. Our position descriptions also list a contact person for job specific inquiries. Let our staff tell you more. 0:00 / 4:17 About us Established in 1870 Federation University has been reaching communities and building generations of independent thinkers united in the knowledge that they are greater together. Federation University is committed to attracting, developing and retaining the best talent ranging from our academic and research staff to those working in student experience and professional roles. We are all part of a collaborative culture inspiring the highest levels of excellence, innovation, integrity and respect. Read More Follow Us Federation University Information Privacy Procedure © 2026 Workday, Inc. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://wd105.myworkdaysite.com/recruiting/federation/Federation_Careers/job/Ballarat-Victoria/Lecturer--Early-Childhood-Education_JR101317": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Early Childhood Education",
      "description": "Lecturer, Early Childhood Education Skip to main content Federation Careers Sign In Working at Federation Search for Jobs Introduce Yourself Lecturer, Early Childhood Education page is loaded Lecturer, Early Childhood Education Apply locations Ballarat, Victoria Berwick, Victoria time type Full time posted on Posted 6 Days Ago time left to apply End Date: September 21, 2026 (5 days left to apply) job requisition id JR101317 Actively engage in teaching and student engagement related activities within the discipline of Initial Teacher Education. •\tInstitute of Education, Arts and Community – Mt Helen or Berwick Campus •\tX2 full-time, continuing appointments •\tAcademic Level B - $116,527 p.a. plus up to 17% superannuation Position closing date: 20/09/2026 Ranked number one university in Australia for First Generation Student Enrolments (Good Universities Guide 2022) and with top rankings in Victoria around student support, social equity, skills and employment, we are driven to make difference to every student and the community providing lifelong learning, skills, and research locally, regionally, and globally. With University and TAFE campuses in Ballarat, Berwick, Gippsland, and the Wimmera we are positioned to provide pathways from vocational education and skills training through to higher education. About the role As an integral member of our team, you will contribute to the development, delivery and assessment of Early Childhood Education units at undergraduate and graduate levels and contribute to the institute by undertaking scholarly research and administrative functions. You will: prepare and deliver lectures, tutorials and seminars; undertake assessment and moderation of units at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; develop course materials and resources in early childhood education; and contribute to a range of activities associated with the development and delivery of curriculum. About you You will work as part of the Institute’s team of academic and administrative staff. You will possess proven educational, scholarly research and professional experience and seek to make a solid contribution to the teaching effort within the Institute within the strategic framework of the University and in accordance with its mission. You will be a creative thinker and avid problem-solver, who possesses initiative, innovation, and a can-do attitude. You will possess demonstrated: commitment to and enthusiasm for teaching with a strong record of teaching experience in a tertiary environment; ability to develop and implement a student-centred approach with a focus on student educational experience and success; experience in academic administration; and ability, commitment and passion for engaging in scholarly research. All University positions delivering education and/or services to children must hold a valid Working With Children Check (WWCC). Please refer to the position description for WWCC requirements. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are strongly encouraged to apply. How to apply Please apply by Sunday, 20 September 2026 Applicants are required to submit a suitability statement not to exceed two-pages and a resume. View position description Federation University is committed to The Circle Back Initiative program, whereby we will respond to every applicant. If you are experiencing technical difficulties with your application, please email the Recruitment team or phone 03 5327 9756. Our position descriptions also list a contact person for job specific inquiries. Let our staff tell you more. 0:00 / 4:17 About us Established in 1870 Federation University has been reaching communities and building generations of independent thinkers united in the knowledge that they are greater together. Federation University is committed to attracting, developing and retaining the best talent ranging from our academic and research staff to those working in student experience and professional roles. We are all part of a collaborative culture inspiring the highest levels of excellence, innovation, integrity and respect. Read More Follow Us Federation University Information Privacy Procedure © 2026 Workday, Inc. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://wd105.myworkdaysite.com/recruiting/federation/Federation_Careers/job/Berwick-Victoria/Associate-Professor--Physiotherapy_JR101390": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, Physiotherapy",
      "description": "Associate Professor, Physiotherapy Skip to main content Federation Careers Sign In Working at Federation Search for Jobs Introduce Yourself Associate Professor, Physiotherapy page is loaded Associate Professor, Physiotherapy Apply locations Berwick, Victoria Gippsland, Victoria time type Full time posted on Posted Today time left to apply End Date: October 5, 2026 (18 days left to apply) job requisition id JR101390 Provide leadership in the development and delivery of Physiotherapy programs and courses. •\tInstitute of Health and Wellbeing –Berwick or Gippsland Campus •\tFull-time, continuing appointment •\tAcademic Level D - $170,875 p.a. plus up to 17% superannuation Position closing date: 04/10/2026 Ranked number one university in Australia for First Generation Student Enrolments (Good Universities Guide 2022) and with top rankings in Victoria around student support, social equity, skills and employment, we are driven to make difference to every student and the community providing lifelong learning, skills, and research locally, regionally, and globally. With University and TAFE campuses in Ballarat, Berwick, Gippsland, and the Wimmera we are positioned to provide pathways from vocational education and skills training through to higher education. About the role As an integral member of our team, you will contribute and provide leadership to the development and delivery of Physiotherapy programs and courses at undergraduate and graduate levels. You will also be expected to contribute to the Institutes research program and administrative functions. You will: make significant contribution to develop, teach, coordinate and moderate courses; provide leadership for the development, implementation and monitoring of student retention and success strategies; play a leadership role in the teaching, research and administrative functions of the Institute; and make an outstanding contribution to research activity within the Institute. About you You will have excellent interpersonal, oral and written communications skills and an ability to relate well to a diverse range of students. You will have enthusiasm for teaching and learning that is accompanied by distinguished teaching record and research experience. You will also possess the ability to work both independently and as part of a team as well as capability to supervise honours and research postgraduate students. All University positions must hold a valid Employee Working With Children Check (WWCC). Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are encouraged to apply How to apply Please apply by Sunday, 4 October 2026. Applicants are required to submit a resume and a suitability statement not to exceed two-pages. View position description Federation University is committed to The Circle Back Initiative program, whereby we will respond to every applicant. If you are experiencing technical difficulties with your application, please email the Recruitment team or phone 03 5327 9756. Our position descriptions also list a contact person for job specific inquiries. Let our staff tell you more. About us Established in 1870 Federation University has been reaching communities and building generations of independent thinkers united in the knowledge that they are greater together. Federation University is committed to attracting, developing and retaining the best talent ranging from our academic and research staff to those working in student experience and professional roles. We are all part of a collaborative culture inspiring the highest levels of excellence, innovation, integrity and respect. Read More Follow Us Federation University Information Privacy Procedure © 2026 Workday, Inc. All rights reserved."
